=== 2026-09-07 IPv6 routed design (dormant until upstream GUA) ===
FINDINGS: phone dnsmasq 2.51 is v4-ONLY (101-line help, zero v6/RA symbols)
-> no dnsmasq RA/DHCPv6 possible. Upstream High5 offers NO global v6
(wlan0 link-local only); SmartRG earlier showed GUA 2604:... + ULA.
DESIGN (no NAT, mirrors v4): same-LAN /64 model. a32radvd.py (new, stdlib
only, --selftest proves framing+checksum+fields offline) multicasts RA
(PIO L+A, MTU, SLLAO, router lifetime tied to upstream-default presence)
+ answers RS. a32routerd route6_ensure per tick: detect first GUA /64,
table 100 v6 (LAN connected + default copied from upstream + NO main-table
dependence — v6 has the same 32000-unreachable bypass), rules 5000/5001
(verified free in v6 namespace), ip6tables a32fwd6 (interface-pair, stable
across prefix changes), proxy_ndp switch + per-address proxy sweep with
stale cleanup, radvd lifecycle via pidfile (+cmdline-verified adoption),
transitions logged, loss-of-prefix tears everything down.
PC: SLAAC stable-EUI64 (addr-gen-mode eui64, tempaddr off), metric-700
default, v4 DNS covers AAAA too (no RDNSS needed). No RDNSS/DHCPv6 by
design (unavailable server-side, unnecessary client-side).
VERIFIED DORMANT on High5: status up, v4 ping OK, no v6 rules/table/proxy/
radvd/prefix-file; PC profile set, no v6 addr (link-local only).
NOT YET PROVEN E2E (needs upstream GUA = SmartRG window).

=== 2026-09-07 E2E verdict: LAN-grade v6 PROVEN, internet gated upstream ===
PHONE->PC echo: 2/2 replies 0.7 ms (type 129 matched). Full path proven:
to-rule -> table 100 -> /128 dev rndis0 -> ND -> PC answers -> back.
ROOT-CAUSE LOG (each cost a wrong turn):
- `ip route show` OMITS /128 suffix on host routes (v6) and /32 (v4). Grep
  for "^addr " (bare + trailing space), never "^addr/128". Caused phantom
  "missing route" + WARN spam; route was present all along.
- Kernel neigh table does NOT reliably show the PC's global (multicast ND
  visibility). Discovery = deterministic EUI-64 from the pinned v4 neighbor
  MAC + sweep supplement (tempaddr/manual extras).
- stpbt-style lesson repeated: tcpdump-to-file must outlive `timeout`
  (read AFTER expiry) or the capture reads empty.
- Link-local cross-link ping is UNFIXABLE by design (fe80::/64 ambiguous
  across links; policy routing sends replies out wlan0 per wlan0_local).
  Always test globals; document, don't chase.
- PC->global blocked LOCALLY: ProtonVPN IPv6 leak protection REJECTs all
  outbound global v6 (instant port-unreachable from own stack; LL exempt
  which is why v4+LL behaved differently). Needs operator VPN action.
- Upstream SmartRG advertises GUA /64 but NO default route (kernel ground
  truth: only dummy0 default anywhere) -> no v6 transit for anyone,
  including the phone itself. Needs router/ISP side.
FINAL MATRIX: RA->SLAAC, proxy, /128, rules, table, forwarding, firewall,
dormant mode, transitions, uninstall coverage: all proven live. PC->phone
and internet-v6: externally gated (VPN / upstream), mechanisms ready.

=== 2026-09-07 zone verdict + ghost false alarm ===
USER REPORT: internet dies when a32static moved to public zone.
FINDING: zone innocent. Journal proves activation SUCCEEDED with the changed
zone (all states to `activated`), then user disconnected manually twice;
autoconnect=no kept it down. Reactivated -> fully working. Zones don't filter
outbound; public and a32phone behave identically for this use.
FALSE ALARM (own goal): `pgrep -f a32radvd` matched the querying shell itself
-> reported a ghost that never existed. Bracket-pattern discipline applies to
READ checks too, not just kills. Verified clean via bracket-safe scan.
Hardening kept anyway: radvd_stop pattern-kills + dormant branch always
stops (cheap orphan insurance).
